## Why This Is Asked
Tests data residency, tenant isolation, and end-to-end security in real-time inference.

## Key Concepts
- PrivateLink isolation and per-tenant KMS envelopes
- Tenant-scoped Feature Store and de-identification
- Canary rollouts and drift monitoring
- Rollback criteria and latency targets

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo preprocessor: drop PII, hash identifiers
function preprocess(input, tenantId){
  const deid = deidentify(input);
  const keys = kms.getTenantKey(tenantId);
  return envelopeEncrypt(deid, keys);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test per-tenant key rotation without service interruption?
- What metrics would you use to trigger automatic rollbacks?
- How would you handle cross-tenant model version drift detection?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests lifecycle management, reproducibility, and safe feature releases in a privacy-conscious SageMaker setup.

## Key Concepts

- SageMaker Experiments and Model Registry
- Canary deployments and rollback strategies
- Drift and quality monitoring with lightweight checks
- PrivateLink isolation and VPC security

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: create an Experiment and a Trial
import { SageMakerClient, CreateExperimentCommand, CreateTrialCommand } from "@aws-sdk/client-sagemaker";
const c = new SageMakerClient({region: 'us-east-1'});
async function init() {
  const exp = await c.send(new CreateExperimentCommand({ExperimentName: 'TextClassifier_V1'}));
  await c.send(new CreateTrialCommand({TrialName: 'V1_Run', ExperimentName: exp.ExperimentArn}));
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you automate canary rollback if latency exceeds threshold for 3 consecutive windows?
- What minimal drift signals would trigger a new model version in the registry?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical implementation of SageMaker for anomaly detection, focusing on real-time latency requirements, data residency constraints, and phased deployment strategies using canary releases.

## Key Concepts
- Anomaly detection models (Isolation Forest, autoencoders)
- Time-series feature engineering (rolling windows)
- Endpoint configuration and autoscaling (min/max instances, latency targets)
- Monitoring and drift detection (SageMaker Clarify, CloudWatch)
- Cost optimization and regional data compliance

